Interactive Visual Analytics
============================
Interactive visual analytics 
> enables users to explore and manipulate data in an interactive and real-time way
> users can find visual patterns faster and more effectively
> interactive data visualisation or dashboarding can tell a more appealing story

Common interactions include:
> zoom-in and zoom-out 
> pan
> filter
> search
> link

***Folium and Ploty Dash will be used to build interactive map and dashboard***

> Folium to analyse launch site geo and proximities 
  - mark launch sites and their close proximities on an interactive map
  - explore the map with those markers and try to discover patterns
  - explain how to choose an optimal launch site

> Plotly Dash to build a dashboard application
  - includes input components including dropdown list and a range slider to interact with a pie chart and a scatter point chart


Task 1  Mark all launch sites on a map
======================================
#Summarise the coordinates for each launch site
-------------
# Select relevant sub-columns: `Launch Site`, `Lat(Latitude)`, `Long(Longitude)`, `class`
spacex_df = spacex_df[['Launch Site', 'Lat', 'Long', 'class']]
launch_sites_df = spacex_df.groupby(['Launch Site'], as_index=False).first()
launch_sites_df = launch_sites_df[['Launch Site', 'Lat', 'Long']]
launch_sites_df

#Create folium circles
-------------
# Create a blue circle at NASA Johnson Space Center's coordinate with a popup label showing its name
circle = folium.Circle(nasa_coordinate, radius=1000, color='#d35400', fill=True).add_child(folium.Popup('NASA Johnson Space Center'))
# Create a blue circle at NASA Johnson Space Center's coordinate with a icon showing its name
marker = folium.map.Marker(
    nasa_coordinate,
    # Create an icon as a text label
    icon=DivIcon(
        icon_size=(20,20),
        icon_anchor=(0,0),
        html='<div style="font-size: 12; color:#d35400;"><b>%s</b></div>' % 'NASA JSC',
        )
    )
site_map.add_child(circle)
site_map.add_child(marker)

#Initiate the map
-------------
site_map = folium.Map(location=nasa_coordinate, zoom_start=5)

#Create Circle objects for each sites
-------------
for index, row in launch_sites_df.iterrows():
    circle = folium.Circle(location=[row['Lat'],row['Long']], radius=1000, color='#d35400', fill=True).add_child(folium.Popup(row['Launch Site']))
    circle.add_to(site_map)

site_map.save('site_map_with_circle.html')

Task 2  Mark the success/failed launches for each site on the map
=================================================================
#Classify marker colors
-------------
spacex_df['marker_color']=None

for index, row in spacex_df.iterrows():
    if row['class'] == 1: 
        spacex_df.loc[index,'marker_color']='green'
    elif row['class'] == 0:
        spacex_df.loc[index,'marker_color']='red'
    
# Apply a function to check the value of `class` column
# If class=1, marker_color value will be green
# If class=0, marker_color value will be red
spacex_df.tail(10)

#Create Marker Cluster and Marker Objects
-------------
# Add marker_cluster to current site_map
site_map.add_child(marker_cluster)

# for each row in spacex_df data frame
# create a Marker object with its coordinate
# and customize the Marker's icon property to indicate if this launch was successed or failed, 
# e.g., icon=folium.Icon(color='white', icon_color=row['marker_color']
for index, record in spacex_df.iterrows():
    # TODO: Create and add a Marker cluster to the site map
    marker=folium.map.Marker(location=[record['Lat'],record['Long']],
                             popup = record['Launch Site'],
                             icon=folium.Icon(color='white',icon_color=record['marker_color'], icon='info-sign'))
    # marker = folium.Marker(...)
    marker_cluster.add_child(marker)

site_map

#Save site map with markers
-------------
site_map.save('site_map_with_marker_cluster_v2.html')


